{"step_index":220,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-13T06:24:01Z","input_tokens":3000,"cache_read_tokens":109535,"output_tokens":2251,"thinking":"Kezza business journey test confirmed successful backend operation, validating every HTTP request and business rule. Agent registration generates a unique referral code and link. Patient registration with the agent's code triggers referral attribution, locking the referral on both agent and patient sides.\n\n\nThe mobile app frontend structure is established, including API client configuration with authentication and user state management. Hooks are identified for handling authentication flows (requesting and verifying OTP, user registration, and current user retrieval) and referral-related actions. The next step is to update referral hooks to include actions for creating and retrieving referral data.\n\n\nThe mobile app API hooks are defined for referral management, patient wallet, and purchase treatment functionalities. The login screen facilitates phone number entry and optional referral code input, followed by OTP verification. If a new user is detected, the verification screen offers inline registration, saving the authentication token upon successful registration.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"import * as SecureStore from 'expo-secure-store';\nimport { Platform } from 'react-native';\nimport { create } from 'zustand';\n\nexport type UserRole = 'patient' | 'agent';\n\nexport interface AuthUser {\n  id: string;\n  fullName: string;\n  phone: string;\n  role: UserRole;\n  agentCode?: string;\n  patientId?: string;\n  agentId?: string;\n  email?: string;\n}\n\nexport interface SignInPayload {\n  accessToken: string;\n  user: AuthUser;\n}\n\ninterface AuthState {\n  isHydrated: boolean;\n  isAuthenticated: boolean;\n  accessToken: string | null;\n  user: AuthUser | null;\n  pendingReferralCode: string | null;\n\n  hydrate: () => Promise<void>;\n  signIn: (payload: SignInPayload) => Promise<void>;\n  signOut: () => Promise<void>;\n  setPendingReferralCode: (code: string | null) => void;\n  updateUser: (user: Partial<AuthUser>) => void;\n}\n\nconst KEYS = {\n  token: 'kezza_access_token',\n  user: 'kezza_user',\n} as const;\n\nasync function secureGet(key: string): Promise<string | null> {\n  if (Platform.OS === 'web') return localStorage.getItem(key);\n  try {\n    return await SecureStore.getItemAsync(key);\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function secureSet(key: string, value: string): Promise<void> {\n  if (Platform.OS === 'web') {\n    localStorage.setItem(key, value);\n    return;\n  }\n  try {\n    await SecureStore.setItemAsync(key, value);\n  } catch {\n    // Ignore storage errors on restricted environments\n  }\n}\n\nasync function secureDelete(key: string): Promise<void> {\n  if (Platform.OS === 'web') {\n    localStorage.removeItem(key);\n    return;\n  }\n  try {\n    await SecureStore.deleteItemAsync(key);\n  } catch {\n    // Ignore\n  }\n}\n\nexport const useAuthStore = create<AuthState>((set, get) => ({\n  isHydrated: false,\n  isAuthenticated: false,\n  accessToken: null,\n  user: null,\n  pendingReferralCode: null,\n\n  hydrate: async () => {\n    try {\n      const [token, userJson] = await Promise.all([\n        secureGet(KEYS.token),\n        secureGet(KEYS.user),\n      ]);\n\n      if (token && userJson) {\n        const user: AuthUser = JSON.parse(userJson);\n        set({ isAuthenticated: true, accessToken: token, user });\n      }\n    } catch {\n      // Corrupted storage — treat as signed out\n    } finally {\n      set({ isHydrated: true });\n    }\n  },\n\n  signIn: async ({ accessToken, user }) => {\n    await Promise.all([\n      secureSet(KEYS.token, accessToken),\n      secureSet(KEYS.user, JSON.stringify(user)),\n    ]);\n    set({ isAuthenticated: true, accessToken, user });\n  },\n\n  signOut: async () => {\n    await Promise.all([\n      secureDelete(KEYS.token),\n      secureDelete(KEYS.user),\n    ]);\n    set({ isAuthenticated: false, accessToken: null, user: null });\n  },\n\n  setPendingReferralCode: (code: string | null) => {\n    set({ pendingReferralCode: code });\n  },\n\n  updateUser: (updatedFields: Partial<AuthUser>) => {\n    const current = get().user;\n    if (current) {\n      const updated = { ...current, ...updatedFields };\n      set({ user: updated });\n      secureSet(KEYS.user, JSON.stringify(updated));\n    }\n  },\n}));\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"/Users/ravi/Desktop/Kezza_mobile-main/src/store/auth-store.ts"}}]}
